# Tenant SMS cancel closes Active Tasks

When a tenant cancels a repair over SMS (after YES, when required), Ulo must close **both** the work order and the Active Tasks card. Ticket status alone is not enough.

## Rule

| Layer | Required close |
|---|---|
| Work order | `maintenance_requests.vendor_work_status = cancelled`, unassign vendor |
| Active Tasks | Linked `workflow_runs` (`maintenance_intake` and `maintenance_request`) → `status = cancelled` |
| SMS thread | Release the intake pin so the next text is not stuck on that wizard |

Intake runs are often keyed to the **SMS conversation**, not the ticket. Always resolve the ticket from `entity_id` **or** `metadata.draft_ticket_id` / `metadata.maintenance_request_id`.

Cancelled ≠ completed vendor work. Do **not** leave cancelled jobs in New Intake, Assigned, or In Progress. Hide them from Active Tasks (and property/resident workflow lists) when `run.status === cancelled` **or** `vendor_work_status === cancelled`.

Bare `Cancel` remains the carrier STOP keyword. Work-order cancel uses phrases like “Cancel it” / “Never mind”, then YES when a ticket already exists.

When Ulo asks which request to cancel, naming that request **is** the confirmation — do not treat the quote as “No” and leave the work order open.

If two open tickets share the **same title** (intake restart duplicates), they are one request: list it once, and quoting that title cancels it. Do not send the same “which one?” SMS again. Mid-intake “Never mind” / “Cancel it” is the **current** request — do not ask the tenant to pick among duplicate titles.

## Where it lives

- Close path: `closeWorkOrderCancelledByResident` in `_shared/sms/cancelResidentWorkOrder.ts`
- SMS act: `handleCancel` in `inboundInterpretationAct.ts`
- Board filter: `isCancelledOnActiveTasks` / `maintenanceTicketIdFromWorkflowRun` in `src/lib/adminWorkflows.ts`

## Do not

- Update only the ticket and leave the workflow run `active`
- Ask “which one?” again after the resident named a request whose title appears twice
- List the same request twice in the which-one SMS
- List **status-question** tickets (e.g. “Who is coming to fix…?”) as cancelable repairs — see `sms-false-work-order-tickets.mdc`
- Treat cancelled jobs as completed vendor work on the kanban
- Add a new inbound SMS registry handler for cancel
